        "closed_at": "2025-01-01T15:19:13Z",
        "author_association": "NONE",
        "active_lock_reason": null,
        "body": "### Preflight Checklist\r\n\r\n- [X] I use the latest version of YouTube Music (Application).\r\n- [X] I have searched the [issue tracker](https://github.com/th-ch/youtube-music/issues) for a feature request that matches the one I want to file, without success.\r\n\r\n### Problem Description\r\n\r\nEnhancing #2767\r\n\r\nThis thing didn't get putting song just after current one. It is pretty useful, i.e. for streamers, so people request a song and it is played just after one from streamer's queue is completed.\r\n\r\n### Proposed Solution\r\n\r\nBy researching source code, I found that enum is already prepared for making such a thing\r\nhttps://github.com/th-ch/youtube-music/blob/85d1dc46d120ace62f2f9d18dce5404ba2a5838f/src/types/datahost-get-state.ts#L431\r\n\r\n### Alternatives Considered\r\n\r\nI'm not sure for any alternatives, cause even building external API with calling all the methods like /api/v1/queue is way more complicated for me. Because even checking for current playing song's position in queue takes a lot of conditions. \r\n\r\n### Additional Information\r\n\r\n_No response_",
