        "body": "_:hammer_and_wrench: Refactor suggestion_\n\n**Consider implementing pagination for collection arrays**\n\nThe current implementation exposes full arrays for `answerCollections`, `sharedCollections`, and `requestedCollections`. This could lead to performance issues with large datasets. Consider:\n1. Implementing cursor-based pagination\n2. Adding limit/offset parameters\n3. Using connection types following Relay specifications\n\n\nExample implementation:\n\n```typescript\nexport const UserAnswerCollections = UserAnswerCollectionsRef.implement({\n  fields: (t) => ({\n    answerCollections: t.field({\n      type: [AnswerCollectionRef],\n      args: {\n        first: t.arg.int(),\n        after: t.arg.string({ nullable: true }),\n      },\n      resolve: async (parent, args) => {\n        // Implement cursor-based pagination\n      },\n    }),\n    // Similar implementation for other collections\n  }),\n})\n```\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit -->",
