        "body": "**Actionable comments posted: 4**\n\n<details>\n<summary>🧹 Nitpick comments (13)</summary><blockquote>\n\n<details>\n<summary>apps/frontend-manage/src/components/resources/SharedAnswerCollectionList.tsx (2)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`5-5`: **Remove the empty object destructuring in the function signature.**  \nSince no properties are explicitly destructured, it’s unnecessary to include `{}` in the parameter.  \n\n\n```diff\n-function SharedAnswerCollectionList({}: {\n+function SharedAnswerCollectionList({\n   sharedCollections?: AnswerCollection[]\n   requestedCollections?: AnswerCollection[]\n   loading: boolean\n }) {\n```\n\n<details>\n<summary>🧰 Tools</summary>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🪛 Biome (1.9.4)</summary>\n\n[error] 5-5: Unexpected empty object pattern.\n\n\n\n(lint/correctness/noEmptyPattern)\n\n</details>\n\n</details>\n\n---\n\n`12-13`: **Implement the placeholder functionality.**  \nThere’s a TODO comment indicating that the shared answer collection list content will be added. Consider addressing this sooner to avoid forgetting the planned feature.\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>apps/frontend-manage/src/components/resources/AnswerCollectionCollapsible.tsx (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`13-13`: **Make the default open state configurable.**  \nDepending on UX requirements, consider allowing a prop (e.g., `defaultOpen?: boolean`) to control the initial expand/collapse state, improving flexibility across different use cases.\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>apps/frontend-manage/src/components/resources/AnswerCollectionList.tsx (2)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`8-8`: **Schedule or implement the editing mechanism.**  \nA TODO suggests adding an editing feature. Plan or implement it soon to avoid merging incomplete functionality without a clear timeline.\n\n---\n\n`14-16`: **Validate loading vs. collections usage.**  \nEnsure the `loading` state properly guards or indicates when `collections` might be undefined or still loading. For clarity, you might want to skip rendering `collections` entirely when `loading` is true.\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>apps/frontend-manage/src/components/resources/AnswerCollectionItem.tsx (2)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`25-44`: **Consider externalizing or reusing the access map.**  \nIf multiple components will rely on mapping `CollectionAccess` to UI representations, refactor this map into a shared utility to avoid duplicating logic.\n\n---\n\n`46-85`: **Potential UX improvement for read-only mode.**  \nWhen `editable` is false, consider clarifying the user flow for viewing shared content, possibly using a tooltip or additional text for consistency with the displayed “VIEW SHARED CONTENT” button text.\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>apps/frontend-manage/src/components/resources/AnswerCollections.tsx (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`1-33`: **Handle loading and error states for better user experience.**  \nCurrently, the UI simply destructures `data` and `loading` from the query without handling errors or providing a fallback loader/spinner. Consider explicitly handling `error` using `useQuery` or showing a loading indicator to enhance user feedback.  \n\n```diff\n function AnswerCollections() {\n   const t = useTranslations()\n-  const { data, loading } = useQuery(GetAnswerCollectionsDocument)\n+  const { data, loading, error } = useQuery(GetAnswerCollectionsDocument)\n\n   if (loading) {\n+    return <div>Loading collections...</div>\n   }\n\n+  if (error) {\n+    return <div>Error loading collections: {error.message}</div>\n+  }\n```\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>packages/graphql/src/services/resources.ts (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`111-113`: **Consider clarifying null returns for missing users.**  \nIn GraphQL, returning `null` for unauthorized or non-existent users is common, but a more specific error can help the client distinguish between an actual permission problem and a missing user. If this is intentional, it’s fine; otherwise, consider a custom exception or a user-friendly message.\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>packages/graphql/src/ops.schema.json (2)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`823-930`: **Add descriptions and consider field constraints.**\n\nThe new types lack descriptions and field-level documentation. Additionally:\n1. Consider making `ownerShortname` required for proper access control.\n2. Consider adding validation constraints (e.g., min/max length) for string fields like `name`, `description`, and `value`.\n\n\nExample improvements:\n\n```diff\n {\n   \"kind\": \"OBJECT\",\n   \"name\": \"AnswerCollection\",\n-  \"description\": null,\n+  \"description\": \"Represents a collection of answers that can be shared between users\",\n   \"fields\": [\n     {\n       \"name\": \"name\",\n-      \"description\": null,\n+      \"description\": \"The name of the collection (1-100 characters)\",\n       ...\n     },\n     {\n       \"name\": \"ownerShortname\",\n       \"type\": {\n-        \"kind\": \"SCALAR\",\n+        \"kind\": \"NON_NULL\",\n         \"name\": \"String\",\n         ...\n       },\n       ...\n     }\n   ]\n }\n```\n\n\nAlso applies to: 931-974\n\n---\n\n`24132-24215`: **Clarify collection types and add pagination.**\n\nThe `UserAnswerCollections` type needs:\n1. Clear descriptions distinguishing between collection types\n2. Pagination support for each collection list\n3. Consider making lists nullable if they can be empty\n\n\nExample improvements:\n\n```diff\n {\n   \"kind\": \"OBJECT\",\n   \"name\": \"UserAnswerCollections\",\n-  \"description\": null,\n+  \"description\": \"Groups different types of answer collections accessible to a user\",\n   \"fields\": [\n     {\n       \"name\": \"answerCollections\",\n-      \"description\": null,\n+      \"description\": \"Collections owned by the user\",\n       ...\n     },\n     {\n       \"name\": \"requestedCollections\",\n-      \"description\": null,\n+      \"description\": \"Collections the user has requested access to\",\n       ...\n     },\n     {\n       \"name\": \"sharedCollections\",\n-      \"description\": null,\n+      \"description\": \"Collections shared with the user by others\",\n       ...\n     }\n   ]\n }\n```\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>packages/graphql/src/ops.ts (2)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`276-280`: **Consider adding JSDoc comments to document the enum values.**\n\nThe `CollectionAccess` enum is well-defined with appropriate values. Consider adding documentation to clarify the implications of each access level.\n\n\n```diff\n+/**\n+ * Access levels for answer collections\n+ * PRIVATE - Only visible to the owner\n+ * PUBLIC - Visible to all users\n+ * RESTRICTED - Visible to specific users or groups\n+ */\n export enum CollectionAccess {\n   Private = 'PRIVATE',\n   Public = 'PUBLIC',\n   Restricted = 'RESTRICTED'\n }\n```\n\n---\n\n`1102-1102`: **Consider enhancing error handling for GraphQL operations.**\n\nFor robust error handling:\n1. Define specific error types for common failure cases (e.g., duplicate names, invalid access levels).\n2. Implement union types with error variants for mutation responses.\n3. Add error-specific fields in the response types.\n\nThis will help clients handle errors more effectively.\n\nExample implementation:\n\n```typescript\ntype CreateAnswerCollectionResponse = {\n  __typename?: 'CreateAnswerCollectionResponse';\n  collection?: Maybe<AnswerCollection>;\n  error?: Maybe<{\n    code: 'DUPLICATE_NAME' | 'INVALID_ACCESS' | 'UNAUTHORIZED';\n    message: string;\n  }>;\n};\n```\n\n\nAlso applies to: 2207-2207\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>📜 Review details</summary>\n\n**Configuration used: CodeRabbit UI**\n**Review profile: CHILL**\n**Plan: Pro**\n\n<details>\n<summary>📥 Commits</summary>\n\nReviewing files that changed from the base of the PR and between 15b1d924e30689b0d9d03440a4e37cb389d12b83 and b3fb6cf56494b0bfeaf1ce7a91a11065487ef19c.\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>📒 Files selected for processing (17)</summary>\n\n* `apps/frontend-manage/src/components/resources/AnswerCollectionCollapsible.tsx` (1 hunks)\n* `apps/frontend-manage/src/components/resources/AnswerCollectionItem.tsx` (1 hunks)\n* `apps/frontend-manage/src/components/resources/AnswerCollectionList.tsx` (1 hunks)\n* `apps/frontend-manage/src/components/resources/AnswerCollections.tsx` (1 hunks)\n* `apps/frontend-manage/src/components/resources/SharedAnswerCollectionList.tsx` (1 hunks)\n* `apps/frontend-manage/src/components/resources/answerCollections/CreateAddCollection.tsx` (1 hunks)\n* `packages/graphql/src/graphql/ops/QGetAnswerCollections.graphql` (1 hunks)\n* `packages/graphql/src/ops.schema.json` (5 hunks)\n* `packages/graphql/src/ops.ts` (10 hunks)\n* `packages/graphql/src/public/client.json` (2 hunks)\n* `packages/graphql/src/public/schema.graphql` (5 hunks)\n* `packages/graphql/src/public/server.json` (2 hunks)\n* `packages/graphql/src/schema/query.ts` (3 hunks)\n* `packages/graphql/src/schema/resource.ts` (1 hunks)\n* `packages/graphql/src/services/resources.ts` (1 hunks)\n* `packages/i18n/messages/de.ts` (2 hunks)\n* `packages/i18n/messages/en.ts` (2 hunks)\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🚧 Files skipped from review as they are similar to previous changes (1)</summary>\n\n* apps/frontend-manage/src/components/resources/answerCollections/CreateAddCollection.tsx\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🧰 Additional context used</summary>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🪛 Biome (1.9.4)</summary>\n\n<details>\n<summary>apps/frontend-manage/src/components/resources/SharedAnswerCollectionList.tsx</summary>\n\n[error] 5-5: Unexpected empty object pattern.\n\n\n\n(lint/correctness/noEmptyPattern)\n\n</details>\n\n</details>\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🔇 Additional comments (18)</summary>\n\n<details>\n<summary>packages/graphql/src/schema/resource.ts (2)</summary>\n\n`1-6`: **LGTM! Clean enum definition maintaining type safety**\n\nThe `CollectionAccess` enum is well-defined by reusing values from Prisma, ensuring type consistency between the GraphQL schema and database layer.\n\n---\n\n`19-38`: **Clarify ownership requirements**\n\nThe `ownerShortname` is marked as nullable, which could lead to ownership ambiguity. Consider:\n1. Making it required for certain access levels (e.g., RESTRICTED)\n2. Adding documentation about when it can be null\n3. Adding ownership validation in the resolvers\n\n\n\nRun this script to analyze ownership handling:\n\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>apps/frontend-manage/src/components/resources/SharedAnswerCollectionList.tsx (1)</summary>\n\n`14-20`: **Leverage the props or remove them if unneeded.**  \nCurrently, `sharedCollections`, `requestedCollections`, and `loading` are declared but not used within the component. Either use them to render the appropriate UI or remove if unneeded.\n\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>packages/graphql/src/schema/query.ts (1)</summary>\n\n`816-823`: **Ensure comprehensive test coverage for the new query.**  \nThe newly introduced `getAnswerCollections` query appears logically consistent, but please confirm that unit or integration tests are added to verify both successful retrievals and expected null/error returns when the user context is invalid.\n\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>packages/graphql/src/graphql/ops/QGetAnswerCollections.graphql (1)</summary>\n\n`1-33`: **Query structure looks consistent and complete.**  \nThe fields fetched (e.g., `answerCollections`, `sharedCollections`, `requestedCollections`) and their subfields align well with the new schema. This helps ensure all data is acquired in a single call.\n\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>packages/graphql/src/services/resources.ts (1)</summary>\n\n`28-30`: **Avoid silent null returns when detecting duplicate names.**  \nReturning `null` may not provide enough client feedback if a collection with the same name already exists. Consider throwing an error or returning a more explicit message.\n\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>packages/graphql/src/public/client.json (1)</summary>\n\n`15-15`: **LGTM! The new methods are correctly added.**\n\nThe new methods `CreateAnswerCollection` and `GetAnswerCollections` are properly added with their corresponding hash values, maintaining alphabetical order in the JSON structure.\n\n\n\nAlso applies to: 112-112\n\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>packages/graphql/src/public/schema.graphql (2)</summary>\n\n`85-92`: **LGTM! The new types are well-structured.**\n\nThe new types are properly defined with appropriate fields and relationships:\n- `AnswerCollection` includes essential fields for managing collections\n- `AnswerCollectionEntry` provides a simple structure for answer values\n- `CollectionAccess` enum defines clear access levels\n- `UserAnswerCollections` properly separates different collection types\n\n\n\nAlso applies to: 94-97, 235-239, 1647-1651\n\n---\n\n`1011-1011`: **LGTM! The operations are correctly defined.**\n\nThe new operations are properly integrated:\n- Mutation `createAnswerCollection` with required parameters\n- Query `getAnswerCollections` returning the appropriate type\n\n\n\nAlso applies to: 1420-1420\n\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>packages/i18n/messages/en.ts (1)</summary>\n\n`1796-1842`: **LGTM! The translations are comprehensive and well-structured.**\n\nThe new translations under the `resources` section:\n- Are logically organized and grouped\n- Cover all UI elements and user interactions\n- Include clear error messages and tooltips\n- Follow consistent naming patterns\n- Provide informative descriptions for different access levels\n\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>packages/graphql/src/public/server.json (2)</summary>\n\n`15-15`: **LGTM! CreateAnswerCollection mutation is well-structured.**\n\nThe mutation includes all necessary fields for creating an answer collection and returns appropriate response data including collec