        "body": "This simplifies a lot of conversion code. numpy is widely available. The python list path is very slow and doesn't add much convenience. It might be worth also supporting assigning a list like `o.indices = [1,2]` as well as`o.indices = numpy.array([1, 2])`. Fields and return values should always use numpy arrays where it makes sense.\r\n\r\n- [x] enable numpy by default\r\n- [x] `Py<PyArray>` for struct fields and return types\r\n- [x] optimize converting numpy arrays to Rust \r\n- [x] update pyi type hints for relevant fields and functions\r\n- [x] update examples to show expected dtype",
